<UpdatePage title="A look inside" description="The projects, lessons and useful ideas you'll find in my monthly update." path="/updates/a-look-inside.html" kicker="A sample monthly update">
  <p>Hi, I'm Jevan.</p>
  <p>I built this website to keep a better record of what I'm learning, making and collecting. The monthly update is a way to follow that work without remembering to check the site.</p>
  <p>Here's a sample of what you can expect.</p>
  <h2>What I'm building</h2>
  <p>The website is a project in its own right: a home for my writing, books, projects and adventures. It started with a simple problem—useful things were scattered across too many places.</p>
  <p>The next challenge is making it easy for someone arriving for the first time to find a story worth following. That's why the homepage now puts current work and these updates up front.</p>
  <p><a href="/projects/personal-website.html">See the website project and build notes →</a></p>
  <h2>A question I'm working through</h2>
  <p>How much of a personal website should explain who I am, and how much should show what I'm doing right now?</p>
  <p>My working answer is to give people a short introduction, then something concrete to explore. A project becomes more interesting when you can see the question behind it and what happens next.</p>
  <h2>Something you can use</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/weekly-review-template.html">weekly-review template</a> is a simple way to turn a busy week into lessons and a next step. It asks four things: what happened, what you learned, what matters next, and what you'll commit to.</p>
  <p>Try the last question first: what is the one thing that would make next week meaningful? Write down the next action and give it a place in your calendar.</p>
  <h2>What comes next</h2>
  <p>I'll share progress on the projects I'm working on, the decisions behind them, and useful things I find along the way. You can see the latest snapshot on my <a href="/now.html">Now page</a>.</p>
  <p>What would you like to hear more about? <a href="/contact.html">Send me a note</a>—I'd like to know.</p>
  <p>Jevan</p>
</UpdatePage>
